  ],
  "og_image": "/assets/og/when-the-mission-becomes-the-leader.png",
  "og_image_alt": "When Leaders Make the Work Their Identity: A leader can become so identified with the work that protecting the work slowly becomes protecting himself. TheWrkShop, Leadership & Culture.",
  "scriptures": [
    {
      "ref": "Numbers 20:10",
      "text": "Moses and Aaron gathered the assembly together in front of the rock and Moses said to them, “Listen, you rebels, must we bring you water out of this rock?”"
    },
    {
      "ref": "1 Corinthians 3:7",
      "text": "Neither the one who plants nor the one who waters is anything, but only God, who makes things grow."
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "the_revelation",
      "label": "The Revelation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Listen carefully to Moses:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“Must we bring you water….?”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Moses had been used extraordinarily by God."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Plagues.",
            "Red Sea.",
            "Sinai.",
            "Leadership.",
            "Intercession.",
            "Provision."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But Numbers 20 contains a dangerous moment."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "God is the provider."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Yet Moses speaks:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "“MUST WE….”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The servant and the work can begin blending together."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This doesn’t mean Moses believed he was God."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But it reveals how easy it is for long-term leadership to blur:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "God’s work.",
            "My responsibility.",
            "My contribution.",
            "My identity."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_lie",
      "label": "The Lie",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“THIS CANNOT WORK WITHOUT ME.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Maybe people even tell you that."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "“We need you.”",
            "“Nobody else can do this.”",
            "“You are the vision.”",
            "“You built this.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Be careful."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Because indispensability feels flattering."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But spiritually:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "NEEDING TO BE NEEDED CAN BECOME ITS OWN FORM OF BONDAGE."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If the mission cannot survive without you, one of two things may be true:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The assignment genuinely requires you in this season."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Or:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "you have built dependency instead of leadership."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_truth",
      "label": "The Truth",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "YOU CAN BE IMPORTANT WITHOUT BEING ULTIMATE."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Moses mattered enormously.",
            "Paul mattered.",
            "Peter mattered.",
            "David mattered."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But God’s purposes did not terminate when their assignments ended."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s freeing."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The kingdom existed before us.",
            "The kingdom will continue after us."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "GOD INVITES US INTO HIS WORK. HE DOES NOT HAND US OWNERSHIP OF IT."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That changes leadership."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "when_identity_fuses_with_mission",
      "label": "When Identity Fuses With Mission",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Watch the progression:"
        },
        {
          "type": "flow",
          "steps": [
            "God gives assignment.",
            "Leader becomes fruitful.",
            "People associate work with leader.",
            "Leader receives identity from work.",
            "Threat to work feels like threat to self.",
            "Questions about strategy feel personal.",
            "Succession feels threatening.",
            "Leader cannot imagine releasing control."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Now:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "STEWARDSHIP HAS QUIETLY BECOME OWNERSHIP."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_my_problem",
      "label": "The “My” Problem",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "My church.",
            "My company.",
            "My ministry.",
            "My team.",
            "My people.",
            "My platform."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Sometimes “my” simply means responsibility."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But sometimes it reveals possession."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Ask:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "IF GOD CHOSE TO ADVANCE THIS WITHOUT ME, WOULD I STILL REJOICE?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s a brutal question."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Because it exposes whether I love:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "the mission,",
            "or my place in it."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_audit",
      "label": "The Audit",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullet_list",
          "items": [
            "WHO AM I WITHOUT THIS ROLE?",
            "IF SOMEONE ELSE LED THIS BETTER THAN ME, HOW WOULD I FEEL?",
            "HAVE I CREATED DEPENDENCE ON ME?",
            "DOES EVERYTHING REQUIRE MY APPROVAL?",
            "DO I DEVELOP PEOPLE WHO COULD REPLACE ME?",
            "DOES THE ORGANIZATION KNOW ITS PURPOSE APART FROM MY PERSONALITY?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Then:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "DO I WANT THE MISSION TO WIN, OR DO I NEED TO BE THE ONE WINNING WITH IT?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_surrender",
      "label": "The Surrender",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Say:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“THIS BELONGS TO GOD.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The people.",
            "The organization.",
            "The ministry.",
            "The influence.",
            "The opportunity.",
            "The results."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "My role is stewardship.",
            "Not ownership."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "I will serve faithfully while assigned.",
            "And release faithfully when called."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "take_it_with_you",
      "label": "Take It With You",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "You can be important without being ultimate."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_prayer",
      "label": "The Prayer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Father,"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Thank You for allowing me to participate in Your work."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Forgive me where stewardship has become ownership.",
            "Where assignment has become identity.",
            "Where being useful has become needing to be needed."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Teach me to build what can flourish beyond me.",
            "To develop people.",
            "To release control.",
            "To celebrate fruit I don’t personally produce."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This belongs to You."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "I am a steward.",
            "Not the owner."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "In Jesus name,",
            "Amen."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "hidden_gems",
      "label": "Hidden Gems 💎",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "You can be important without being ultimate."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Needing to be needed can become its own form of bondage."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "God invites us into His work. He does not hand us ownership of it."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Stewardship can quietly become ownership."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Do I want the mission to win, or do I need to be the one winning with it?"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Build what can flourish beyond you."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "-TheWrkShop"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "__insert_block_header": "2026-10-30_numbers-20-10_when-the-mission-becomes-the-leader|"
}
